  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "For operations ProBuilder lacks, a mesh can go to Blender and back. ProBuilder's Export writes the selected mesh as an OBJ file. Blender edits it and exports an FBX file into the Assets folder; Unity imports the file again each time it is saved.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You export the FBX from Blender again, over the same file in Assets. What happens to the copies already in the scene?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select the three pieces of the arch and use Tools \u203A ProBuilder \u203A Export \u203A Export Obj.\n2. Open the file in Blender, change it, and export it as FBX into this sample's Asset-Management/Imports folder.\n3. Change it again in Blender and export over the same file.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Liminal-Kit 1 \xB7 Walls and openings (Arch)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
